**Read:** [Levantamento da geodiversidade — SGB technical guide, volume 5 version 4](../sources/SGB-Geodiversity-Methods.lingua#r_7QW5KYAYK9SB2MT3R6MNCFAQWK), the complete observation/data-method account; [A specimen, a sampling target, and a result about a population](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/metrology/foundations/Sampling-and-representativeness.lingua#r_0F0VEC42GPQPRZM0S7MXF7GAEH), the full shared target and sampling explanation; [Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle](../sources/Physical-Geology-Earle.lingua#r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX), resource and geological-interpretation material; [GeMS — Geologic Map Schema — USGS](../sources/GeMS-Map-Schema.lingua#r_6JP32YH79HZAV8JYYKVV1WER0J), observations, locations, and confidence as applicable.

Exploration combines geological mapping, sampling, geochemistry, geophysics, drilling, logging, and models for a stated question. Each method samples a different property over a different support volume and resolution. A geophysical anomaly is a measured/modelled contrast needing interpretation, not direct proof of a commodity or void.

Drillhole collar coordinates, survey, inclination/azimuth, recovery, depth reference, core orientation, logging, sampling, preparation, assays, and custody affect what the record can establish. Along-hole interval, vertical depth, and true unit thickness differ. A missing core interval is not automatically absent rock or zero grade.

Connect uncertainty in geometry, material classification, sample representativeness, analytical measurement, interpolation, and geological model. A smooth three-dimensional block model can conceal sparse data or unsupported continuity. Cross-validation of nearby samples may overstate prediction quality if spatial dependence and domain definition are ignored.

**Work:** reconstruct an authorized teaching/public drill dataset's observation chain and conceptual model. Relate logs to a section, distinguishing direct intersections and inferred connections. Propose a next observation based on the competing interpretations it can separate, and explain how changed recovery, sample support, or geological domains would alter the inference.

Read the full mapping/sampling methods and relevant resource treatment. Later exploration, geostatistics, geophysics, and mining trails deepen estimation and decisions; general geology should already make the relation between an attractive model, its actual evidence, and unresolved ground conditions inspectable.

**Continue:** [Translate geological history into an explicit ground model for infrastructure questions](Engineering-geology-ground-models-and-observation.lingua#r_0MTDARJP2G6GFXB1Y5HNT00BJ8).

**Return:** [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06).
